Package: nsjail
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: passt
Description: light-weight process isolation tool
 NsJail is a process isolation tool for Linux. It makes use of Linux
 namespaces and seccomp-bpf syscall filters (with help of the kafel
 library) to sandbox processes.
 .
 The suggested passt package provides the pasta(1) binary, which nsjail
 executes for its optional pasta-backed networking mode (user_net.pasta in
 the config). nsjail's other networking modes, e.g. the built-in nstun NAT
 backend, don't need it.
